%% Hopline — how two browsers find each other and open a direct (or relayed) WebRTC connection, plus its lanes.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Alice as Device A (creator)
  participant S as Signaling server
  actor Bob as Device B (joiner)

  Note over Alice,Bob: Each device generates one ECDSA P-256 DTLS certificate per session,<br/>used for the main connection and every lane
  Alice->>S: WebSocket connect /ws (same-origin check)
  Alice->>S: { type: "create" }
  S-->>Alice: { type: "created", code: "K7Q2XM", token, iceServers: STUN }
  Note over Alice: Shows code, QR and invite link

  Bob->>S: WebSocket connect /ws
  Bob->>S: { type: "join", code: "K7Q2XM" }
  Note over S: Wrong codes cost from a per-client budget (10/min)
  S-->>Bob: { type: "joined", code, token, iceServers: STUN + TURN creds }
  S-->>Alice: { type: "peer-joined", iceServers: STUN + TURN creds }

  Note over Alice: Creator is the initiator:<br/>new session id (s1), data channel + offer
  Alice->>S: signal { session, description: offer }
  S->>Bob: signal { session, description: offer }
  Bob->>S: signal { session, description: answer }
  S->>Alice: signal { session, description: answer }

  par ICE candidates (both directions)
    Alice->>S: signal { session, candidate }
    S->>Bob: relay
  and
    Bob->>S: signal { session, candidate }
    S->>Alice: relay
  end

  Alice-)Bob: DTLS handshake (direct, or via TURN relay)
  Note over Alice,Bob: Data channel "hopline" opens → "Connected · Direct/Relayed"<br/>Both show the same 16-digit safety code

  loop Up to 3 lanes, session ids s1.L1 … .L3, 400 ms apart (best effort, 20 s timeout)
    Alice->>S: signal { session: "s1.Ln", description: offer } + ICE
    S->>Bob: relay (accepted only for the current main session)
    Bob->>S: signal { session: "s1.Ln", description: answer } + ICE
    S->>Alice: relay
    Alice-)Bob: DTLS handshake (same route rules, "Hide my IP" included)
    alt Lane's remote DTLS fingerprint == main connection's
      Note over Alice,Bob: Data channel "hopline-lane" carries file frames, badge shows "N lanes"
    else Different certificate (e.g. the server answered itself)
      Note over Alice,Bob: Lane closed with a console warning, never carries data
    end
  end

  opt Either side leaves on purpose
    Bob->>S: { type: "leave" }
    S-->>Alice: { type: "peer-left" }
  end
  opt A connection drops instead
    Note over Alice,Bob: Seat held for the grace period → rejoin + new session (diagram 14)
  end
